The timer makes every core's nearest deadline exact again from the timer lines alone,
so the core that fed the watchdog no longer wakes for it after the first interrupt;
its nearest deadline is no later than the watchdog's.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the watchdog comes due before the timer wakes for it
Witness: fuzz watchdog-halts

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1000,10 +1000,6 @@ void sched_time(uint64_t now)
             kputs("watchdog: not fed in time\n");
             khalt(7);
         }
-        struct core *fed = &cores[watchdog.core];
-        if (watchdog.deadline < fed->nearest_deadline) {
-            fed->nearest_deadline = watchdog.deadline;
-        }
     }
     for (uint32_t c = 0; c < CORES; c++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
